  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish the exact AlCoCrFeNi2.1 alloy's coupled FCC/L12–B2 lamellar structure (especially R8 and R16), show that annealing can alter ordering or phase constitution in related HEAs (R2, R19), and provide general links among ordering, impeded dislocation motion, slip-mode changes, and reduced ductility (R5, R15, R17, R18). Thus they suggest examining temperature-dependent aging of the exact eutectic alloy. However, none identifies intermediate-temperature aging near 600 and 750 °C in this alloy, the maximum in near-stoichiometric L12 ordering, jagged B2/FCC boundaries, the combined APBE/cross-slip and boundary-tip stress-concentration mechanism, or the resulting ductile-brittle-ductile sequence. Reaching the specific intervention and mechanism would therefore require a substantial new idea."
